Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.768
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.260
JOY PAYTON: If you
want to learn how

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.860
to be a data scientist because
you think this is interesting,

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.680
then you definitely need to
be involved with Google Cloud

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.530
platform, because one of
the best ways to learn data

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.390
is using big data.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.930
And there is a great
set of resources for you

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.900
in Google Public data
sets in BigQuery, which is

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.300
a great place to get started.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.110
There's tons of tutorials
that'll help you there

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.340
that are available at no cost.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.730
The hosting of data
sets is at no cost.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:42.010
And all the work that you need
to do can be done in free tier.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:46.890
So there are lots of ways that,
even without participating

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:50.530
in a formal training process
or signing up for an exam,

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:53.970
that you can grow your
skills and really find a data

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.630
set that you're
passionate about.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:58.710
I tell people if you love
sports, look at sports data.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:01.080
If you're concerned
about hunger and poverty,

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.880
look for those data sets.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.800
Find something you care about.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.350
And you will definitely
find some trends that

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.560
make you scratch your
head, or make you angry,

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.480
or make you excited, or
make you ask questions.

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:19.790
So find some data, work with
it, and change the world.

